{
  "_comment": "Snippet for Claude Code ~/.claude/settings.json. Merge the hooks.PreToolUse entry below into your config. The matcher is '.*' by design (fail-safe default): every tool call arrives at guard.sh, which short-circuits an internal stable list of unambiguously read-only tools (Read, Glob, Grep, LS, TodoWrite, WebSearch, ToolSearch) and requires a fresh TOTP session for everything else. This protects new or custom tools by default. To change policy, edit the read-only exit list at the top of /etc/totp-presence/claude-code-guard.sh.",
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": ".*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "/etc/totp-presence/claude-code-guard.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
